+# RQ-0132 — Billing formats and PDF rendering (T-0041)
+
+## Question
+
+- **Q1.** What must the sales tax invoice show (AU GST), including the $1,000 buyer-identity rule?
+- **Q2.** What must the adjustment note (every credit note, T-0045) show?
+- **Q3.** What does the customer statement document show (T-0049 `customerStatement`)?
+- **Q4.** Which engine and library render HTML to PDF at runtime (design §7.1 "HTML templates
+  rendered by headless Chromium")?
+- **Q5.** Can the output be deterministic, so it can be snapshotted and hashed?
+- **Q6.** Tenant data (logo, footer, names) reaches a browser: how is that made safe?
+- **Q7.** Where is the rendered PDF stored? (Card: "via the attachments module from T-0026 if it
+  exists".)
+- **Q8.** How do tests read the text of a PDF without a new runtime dependency?
+- **Q9.** What is the "template record" of design §4.3 as data, and does it need a migration?
+
+## Why it matters
+
+A tax invoice that misses a required field does not let the customer claim its GST credit
+(s 29-10(3), RQ-0095 S4); an adjustment note is required for a decreasing adjustment above $75
+(RQ-0095 S3). A PDF that changes from one render to the next cannot be proved or audited. A
+browser fed tenant text is an injection and SSRF surface.
+
+## Sources
+
+| # | Source | Accessed | Kind | What it says |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
