+
+## Findings
+
+1. **Q1 — tax invoice.** Print, on every posted sales invoice: the title **"Tax invoice"**; the
+   supplier's legal name (company `legal_name`, else `name`) and **ABN** (formatted `51 824 753 556`);
+   the invoice number and **date of issue** (invoice date) and due date; for each line its
+   description, tax code and amount; subtotal, **GST total** and total. Printing the GST amount
+   always satisfies both the amount and the "includes GST" alternative (S1), so the template does
+   not branch on the 1/11 test. For GST-inclusive invoices the total row reads "Total (includes
+   GST)". The buyer's legal name is **always** printed (and its ABN when held): the ≥ $1,000 rule
+   is met for every invoice, with no threshold branch to get wrong. A line's tax code (GST, FRE …)
+   shows the extent each sale is taxable on mixed invoices. A company without an ABN cannot issue
+   a tax invoice: refuse (`NO_SUPPLIER_ABN`). A draft or approved (unnumbered) invoice renders as
+   **"Draft invoice — not a tax invoice"**, never as a tax invoice.
+2. **Q2 — adjustment note.** Title "Adjustment note"; supplier name and ABN; credit-note number and
+   date of issue; recipient legal name (and ABN when held); the reason (brief explanation);
+   original invoice number and date; lines; net, **GST difference** and total. Unposted notes
+   render as "Draft adjustment note".
+3. **Q3 — statement.** Title "Statement"; supplier name and ABN; customer; period from–to; per
+   currency section: opening balance, lines (date, document, due date, debit, credit, balance),
+   closing balance, ageing (current, 1–30, 31–60, 61–90, 90+, unallocated credits, total).
+   Rendered from `customerStatement` unchanged — no arithmetic in the template.
+4. **Q4 — engine.** Use **`playwright-core` 1.63.0** (S5): the same pinned version the e2e suite
+   already resolves, no bundled browser download, Chromium-only `page.pdf`. The Chromium binary
+   is configuration: `LF_CHROMIUM_PATH`, default `/opt/pw-browsers/chromium`. Alternatives:
+   `puppeteer-core` (a second browser driver, new dependency tree, same Chromium), a JS PDF
+   library (`pdfkit`, `pdf-lib`: a second layout engine, so email/preview HTML and PDF would
+   diverge, contrary to S4). Runtime use of a browser is a new runtime dependency → ADR-0046.
+5. **Q5 — determinism.** HTML is a pure function of (document, format) — snapshot it exactly.
+   PDF: set `/CreationDate` and `/ModDate` to the document date (`D:YYYYMMDD000000+00'00'`, same
+   byte length as Chromium's value, so xref offsets stay valid) → identical bytes for identical
+   input on the same Chromium build and fonts (S6a); store the SHA-256. Use **Liberation Sans**
+   (not a variable font) so text is extractable and compact (S6b, S7).
+6. **Q6 — safety.** Every interpolated value is HTML-escaped; the footer is plain text (newlines →
+   `<br>`); the accent colour must match `^#[0-9a-f]{6}$`; the logo is embedded as a `data:` URL
+   only from bytes stored in the format (PNG, JPEG or SVG; ≤ 256 KiB; SVG in `<img>` runs no
+   script). The page runs with JavaScript disabled and **every network request aborted**, so a
+   template can neither run code nor fetch a URL (no SSRF, no tracking pixels).
+7. **Q7 — storage.** No attachments module exists (S8). `renderDocumentPdf` returns the bytes,
+   SHA-256, file name and media type; persisting renditions (object storage, an `attachment`
+   table, the Salesforce "PDF link" field) is follow-up **T-0180**.
+8. **Q8 — text extraction.** `pdftotext` exists here but is not guaranteed in CI. Write a small
+   test-only extractor for the subset Chromium emits (S6d): FlateDecode content streams,
+   Type0/Identity-H fonts with `/ToUnicode` (`bfchar`, `bfrange`), `Tf`/`Tm`/`Td`/`Tj`/`TJ`; a new
+   text line when the baseline moves. Cross-checked against `pdftotext` during development. It
+   lives under `src/testing/` (dev-only, no dependency).
+9. **Q9 — template record.** A tenant-owned table `app.billing_format` (migration 0047): per
+   company, `code`, `name`, `document_kind` (`invoice` | `adjustment_note` | `statement`),
+   `format_kind` (design §4.3 rows), `line_source`, `grouping`, `tax_treatment`, `number_series`,
+   `pdf_layout`, `email_template`, `payment_link`, `is_default` (one default per kind), `logo` +
+   `logo_media_type`, `footer_text`, `accent_color`; RLS ENABLE + FORCE; no DELETE grant (archive
+   with `status`). With no stored format a built-in default is used, so rendering never depends on
+   setup.
+
+## Conclusion
+
+Build `packages/modules/billing` (`@ledgerforce/billing`): billing-format model and store
+(migration 0047), document models built from the AR reads, pure HTML templates, a Chromium
+renderer on `playwright-core` (ADR-0046), and a test-only PDF text extractor. Decisions
